{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight too bright, the colors too saturated. He sat up in bed, a strange, almost rigid feeling to his limbs. The room was…perfect. Too perfect. The meticulously arranged books on the shelf, the precisely placed framed photos, the lack of any dust – it was all unnervingly staged. A notification popped into his vision, a translucent box hovering near his left temple: \"Welcome, Player 472. Level 1: Suburban Awakening. Objective: Complete morning routine.\" He reached out, his hand passing right through the notification. Panic seized him. He looked at his hands – strangely smooth, almost too flawless. He ran to the mirror, and his reflection stared back, a hyper-realistic image of a man he vaguely recognized as himself, but…off. The eyes held a vacant quality, the smile seemed painted on.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of the room, the house stretching out before him in a seamless, almost uncanny valley fashion. The neighbors waved with exaggerated cheerfulness, their movements jerky and repetitive. A quest log appeared in his vision: \"NPC Interaction: Mrs. Gable - Dialogue options: 1. Pleasantry. 2. Inquiry about weather. 3. Request for sugar.\" Arthur felt a wave of nausea. This wasn't real. This couldn't be real. He was trapped inside a video game, a meticulously crafted simulation where his every action was dictated by code. The weight of the objective, the feeling of being a pawn in someone else's design, crushed him. He had to find a way out, to break free from this digital prison, but how could he fight a reality built of ones and zeros?", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.407365083694458}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00015984688070602715}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08786557614803314}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -1.4177302122116089}, {"token": "▁too", 